1 — Protocol Specification (RFC-style) — ShyPal P2P & Cloud Protocol
Version: 1.0 • Date: 2025-11-20
1.1 Goals & assumptions
Primary: enable offline encrypted chat between nearby devices; mutual save creates online friend tokens.


Devices: iOS & Android.


Discovery mediums: BLE Advertising/Scan, Multipeer (iOS), Wi-Fi Aware / Nearby (Android).


Threat model: untrusted opportunistic environment (public spaces). Use E2EE and ephemeral IDs.


1.2 Identifiers
DeviceLongId — Curve25519 public key (long-term, kept private; stored in Secure Enclave / Android Keystore). Not broadcast.


EphemeralBeaconId (EID) — random 32/64-byte value derived from ephemeral Curve25519 public key; rotates every ROTATE_INTERVAL (default 60s). Format: base64url(ECDH_pub || timestamp || capabilities_hash) signed or HMACed by ephemeral private key.


SessionId — UUIDv4 generated when handshake succeeds.


FriendToken — 256-bit random token (base64url) generated upon mutual save; stored locally and optionally registered on backend (encrypted metadata only).


1.3 Crypto primitives
Key agreement: X25519 (Curve25519 ECDH).


KDF: HKDF-SHA256 with context string "ShyPal v1 session".


Symmetric encryption: AES-256-GCM for payloads.


Optional advanced: Signal Protocol (X3DH + Double Ratchet) for full forward secrecy and post-compromise recovery (recommended for Phase 2).


Nonce strategy: 96-bit random nonce per message; include nonce in envelope.


Message MAC: AES-GCM provides integrity.


1.4 Packet formats (over transport adapters)
All packet bytes are binary with small TLV-like framing. For readability show JSON-like structures; final implementation must be binary/CBOR.
1.4.1 Beacon (BLE advertisement payload)
Small payload (<= 31 bytes adv data). Packed fields:
EID_prefix (8 bytes) | version (1 byte) | cap_flags (1 byte) | truncated_ts (4 bytes)

Full ephemeral data retrieved via GATT or Multipeer service discovery when establishing handshake.
1.4.2 IntroRequest (sent when sender taps Send)
{
  type: "intro_req",
  sender_eph_pub: base64url,
  sender_nonce: base64url, // for handshake
  sender_caps: [ "txt" ],
  proto_version: 1
}

1.4.3 IntroReply (recipient)
{
  type: "intro_reply",
  recipient_eph_pub: base64url,
  accept: bool, // if unsolicited allowed = true only for first message
  server_chosen_transport: "BLE" | "WIFI" | "MULTIPEER"
}

1.4.4 EncryptedMessage envelope
Binary envelope:
{
  type: "enc_msg",
  session_id: UUID,
  iv: base64url,
  ciphertext: base64url, // AES-GCM
  seq: uint32, // for ordering
  meta: { display_hint: "one_line" } // optional
}

1.4.5 SaveOffer / SaveConfirm (mutual save)
SaveOffer {
  type: "save_offer",
  session_id: UUID,
  offerer_pub_friend_key: base64url, // new friend pubkey
  optional_profile_blob: base64url // user-chosen emoji, nickname (encrypted to friend key)
}
SaveConfirm {
  type: "save_confirm",
  session_id: UUID,
  confirmer_pub_friend_key: base64url
}

Upon mutual confirm: both parties compute FriendToken = HMAC_SHA256(shared_friend_key, "ShyPalFriendToken") and optionally register public friend prekeys with backend.
1.5 Session lifecycle
Discovery: devices detect EID beacon.


IntroRequest sent (one unsolicited allowed -> recipient sees preview).


If recipient accepts, exchange ephemeral pubs -> derive session key via X25519: sk = HKDF(X25519(sender_eph_priv, recipient_eph_pub) || X25519(sender_long_priv, recipient_eph_pub) || ...). (Use multiple DHs for extra security).


Establish session: assign SessionId.


Exchange messages encrypted with session key.


Track lastActive; if idle > AUTO_DELETE = 5 minutes → delete session keys & payloads.


If SaveOffer occurs and is confirmed → create FriendToken and optional cloud registration.


1.6 Transport & chunking
BLE GATT: chunk ciphertext to 180-byte payloads, reassemble. Provide ACK/resend.


Wi-Fi Direct / Nearby: send full envelope in one payload.


Multipeer: use MCSession data.


1.7 Time & clocking
Use monotonic timers for session TTL. Timestamps only used for debugging and rotate determinism; do not rely on device clock for security.



