5 — Threat Model & Mitigations (prioritized)
5.1 Threats
Stalker tracks user by beacon IDs — BLE beacons can be used for tracking.


Eavesdropper intercepts handshake / messages — man-in-the-middle.


Replay attacks — attacker resends old messages.


Mass spamming — one actor sending many unsolicited messages.


Backend deanonymization — storing tokens or logs that can be correlated.


Device compromise — attacker with physical access obtains saved tokens/messages.


Push spoofing — malicious push to user via compromised server credentials.


5.2 Mitigations (practical)
Rotating Ephemeral IDs (every 60s) & unlinkability by deriving ephemeral IDs from ephemeral keys. Avoid broadcasting long-term pubkeys.


E2EE with X25519 + AES-GCM prevents eavesdropping. Optional Signal Protocol for forward secrecy.


Include nonces and sequence numbers; use HKDF; implement replay protection (reject duplicate seq).


Rate-limiting & one unsolicited message per discovered ephemeral ID; local block list; server-side hashed rate detection.


