6) What to watch out for (real risks & how to mitigate)
BLE / P2P is unreliable across OEMs — test on many devices (Samsung/Xiaomi often have non-standard BLE behaviors). Mitigate: broad device matrix, robust retry/backoff, and platform-specific fallbacks. (Community reports show variability in BLE plugin behavior.) (Stack Overflow)


iOS background discovery is limited — Multipeer requires the app to be running or special entitlements; you can’t run fully stealth background discoverability. Mitigate: clear onboarding UX asking users to open the app when they want to be discoverable. (Apple Developer)


AI hallucinations — AI assistants sometimes generate plausible-but-wrong code. Mitigate: strict code reviews, unit tests, static analysis, and security audit. (Research shows AI can slow experienced devs and needs human oversight.) (Reuters)


Business risk from reliance on closed no-code vendors (Builder.ai cautionary example) — don’t outsource the full product to black-box vendor without code escrow and audit. (Financial Times)



